{"id":"s1","level":5,"levelName":"Structure and style","n":1,"of":14,"title":"Joining clauses","titleHe":"מִשְׁפָּט מְחֻבָּר","goal":"Use שֶׁ, כִּי and כְּדֵי to build sentences longer than one clause.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"שֶׁ is the workhorse. Glued to the front of a clause it does the job of English that, which and who all at once — and unlike English, it is never optional."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אֲנִי חוֹשֵׁב שֶׁהוּא צוֹדֵק.","en":"I think (that) he's right."},{"he":"הָאִישׁ שֶׁבָּא אֶתְמוֹל","en":"the man who came yesterday"},{"he":"הַסֵּפֶר שֶׁקָּרָאתִי","en":"the book (that) I read"},{"he":"כְּשֶׁהִגַּעְתִּי, הוּא כְּבָר הָלַךְ.","en":"When I arrived, he'd already left."}]},{"type":"table","caption":"Connectors","head":["Hebrew","English"],"rows":[["שֶׁ","that, which, who"],["כִּי","because"],["כְּדֵי","in order to"],["אֲבָל","but"],["לִפְנֵי שֶׁ","before"],["אַחֲרֵי שֶׁ","after"],["בִּגְלַל שֶׁ","because of the fact that"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"אֲשֶׁר is שֶׁ in literary dress — same meaning, separate word, and everywhere in older prose. When you meet it, read it as שֶׁ."}],"vocab":[{"he":"שֶׁ","en":"that, which, who","translit":"she-"},{"he":"כִּי","en":"because","translit":"ki"},{"he":"אֲשֶׁר","en":"that, which (literary)","translit":"asher"},{"he":"כְּדֵי","en":"in order to","translit":"kdei"},{"he":"אֲבָל","en":"but","translit":"aval"},{"he":"לָכֵן","en":"therefore","translit":"lachen"},{"he":"לְמָשָׁל","en":"for example","translit":"lemashal"},{"he":"בְּעֶצֶם","en":"actually","translit":"be'etsem"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["bud","electricity","that, which, who","post, mail"],"correct":2,"prompt":"שֶׁ","translit":"she-"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["because","yesterday","after","Hanukkah"],"correct":0,"prompt":"כִּי","translit":"ki"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["looked at","travels","two months","that, which (literary)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אֲשֶׁר","translit":"asher"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["cold","in order to","apartment","while, whereas"],"correct":1,"prompt":"כְּדֵי","translit":"kdei"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["but","fridge","actor, player","really, truly"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אֲבָל","translit":"aval"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["therefore","noon","buys","shoes"],"correct":0,"prompt":"לָכֵן","translit":"lachen"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["to the land","for example","the ninth of Av, a day of mourning","a booth"],"correct":1,"prompt":"לְמָשָׁל","translit":"lemashal"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “for example”?","options":["לְמָשָׁל","בְּלִי","קְרִיאָה","לוּלָב"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “that, which, who”?","options":["הוֹכָחָה","שֶׁ","מִצַּד אֶחָד","עוֹד"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["שֶׁ","בְּעֶצֶם","לָכֵן","אֲשֶׁר"],"correct":3,"say":"אֲשֶׁר","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “that, which (literary)”?","options":["פַּחַד","סֻכָּר","אֲשֶׁר","מִלְּבַד"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “because”?","options":["תַּפּוּז","כִּי","רָקִיעַ","שָׁלֵם"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"הָאִישׁ שֶׁבָּא ___","en":"the man who came yesterday","options":["אֶתְמוֹל","כְּדֵי","לָכֵן","לְמָשָׁל"],"correct":0,"full":"הָאִישׁ שֶׁבָּא אֶתְמוֹל"},{"type":"build","tokens":["חוֹשֵׁב","אֲנִי","שֶׁהוּא","צוֹדֵק"],"answer":["אֲנִי","חוֹשֵׁב","שֶׁהוּא","צוֹדֵק"],"en":"I think (that) he's right."},{"type":"build","tokens":["אֶתְמוֹל","הָאִישׁ","שֶׁבָּא"],"answer":["הָאִישׁ","שֶׁבָּא","אֶתְמוֹל"],"en":"the man who came yesterday"},{"type":"type","q":"Write “but” in Hebrew","answer":"אֲבָל","hint":"aval"}]}